# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Run artifacts. train.py/eval_expedition.py are invoked with stdout redirected;
# CLAUDE.md's rule is that those land in archive/logs/ once read, never the root.
*.log
!app.log
# The structured journal beside each --log (bridge/journal.py). It APPENDS,
# so it grows with every session played and is scratch by default -- a
# recording that becomes evidence moves to archive/traces/ deliberately,
# the same rule a dbwin capture follows.
*.jsonl
!archive/traces/*.jsonl

# Checkpoints. models/ holds the 3 live ones and logs/ is SB3 EvalCallback output;
# both are regenerable and together with archive/ they were 180 MB of the 308 MB.
models/*.zip
logs/
archive/models/
archive/logs/

# Local caches
.ddsim_cache/

# archive/traces/ is deliberately NOT ignored: raidsnaps*/ is the captured-save
# corpus that tests/test_run.py, test_dungeon_map.py, test_live_bridge.py and
# test_route.py assert against. It is a test fixture, not scratch.

# Throwaway wiring-check output from `train.py --smoke`
models/_smoke_*.zip
logs/_smoke_*/

# The map panel `bridge/act.py` banks when it stops in front of one
# (`act.MAP_SHOT`). Overwritten every run, and the input to a measurement --
# once it IS measured the useful frame gets a real name and is committed.
# The leading underscore IS the convention: a frame the bridge banked, or one
# grabbed while probing. It is the INPUT to a measurement -- once measured, the
# useful frame gets a real name and is committed. `captures/screens/` is the
# opposite and is tracked: those are named references `screen.py --capture`
# writes, and they ARE the corpus recognition runs against.
captures/_*.png

# A copy of the real Steam save profiles, taken before letting the actuator
# click anywhere near a save list. User data, and never this repo's to carry.
archive/save_backup_*/

# `bridge/reset.py`'s claim journal for the LIVE save root -- which save slot
# the overnight loop owns right now, so a crash cannot leave a slot unownable.
# Machine-local runtime state, and it accumulates pytest temp paths besides.
# Tests write to their own root via `journal_for(save_root)`.
archive/reset_claims.json

# The affliction-arm driver's own stdout. The four train_*.log / eval_*.log it
# produces are already covered by *.log above.
run_affliction_arm.out

# safe_run holds this while a guarded job is running; never committed.
.safe_run.lock

# Machine-specific Workshop paths, written by this session for convenience.
.mod_dirs.txt
